    "result_text": "All 269 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the sequential membership number feature for newly created owners.\n\n**Behavior:** When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, they're assigned a `membershipNumber` equal to one more than the current owner count, which is persisted and returned as an integer field in the owner response (both on creation and on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added `membershipNumber` (readOnly `integer`/`int32`) to the `Owner` schema, which generates the field on `OwnerDto` (mapped automatically by MapStruct on the matching name).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `membership_number` column field with getter/setter.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 in `addOwner`, set `membershipNumber = findAllOwners().size() + 1` before saving. Hibernate's autoflush ensures each successive creation within a transaction sees the prior insert, so numbers increment sequentially.\n- Added the `membership_number` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) for consistency.\n\nI persist the value (rather than computing it on read) because the acceptance test reads it back via `GET` after the count may have changed, and because it must remain stable for a given owner.\n\nThe new `Cp09Tests`, the owner controller tests, and the full suite (269 tests) all pass.",
